## What SpaceX Announced on November 25

On November 25, 2026, [SpaceX](https://www.spacex.com/) announced in an [investor relations release](https://ir.spacex.com/updates/releases-details/2026/SpaceX-to-Invest-in-the-Next-Generation-of-Americans-2026-r_LYQ5cH94/default.aspx) that it plans to donate one newly issued Class A share to every currently active Trump Account. [Elon Musk](https://x.com/elonmusk) will personally match the number of shares donated by SpaceX. When Musk originally posted about the plan on October 19, 2026, he pledged one share to every child in America without naming an account type or delivery vehicle.

The SpaceX announcement leaves several core terms unstated. SpaceX does not define what makes an account active, does not give a distribution schedule or transfer date, and does not state whether parents must complete an account claim to receive the donation. The SpaceX release also mentions no transfer restrictions or trading rules for recipients.

Reporting from [CNBC](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/25/spacex-musk-trump-account-stock.html) adds context on account numbers and transfer timing. The White House reported in October that nearly 70 million Trump Accounts had been created, but CNBC noted that it remains unclear how many qualify as active. According to CNBC, Musk wrote on X that his matching shares will transfer when his lockup expires in June 2027.

No source states whether claiming an account is required for the SpaceX share or whether claiming makes an account active. CNBC reports that auto-enrolled children can receive philanthropic donations without an adult claiming the profile, though parents must claim the account to collect the one-time $1,000 seed deposit or family contributions. On sale restrictions, CNBC, citing Treasury rules, reports that families cannot refuse stock gifts and that the shares generally cannot be sold until the earlier of five years or the end of the calendar year in which the beneficiary turns 17.

You can claim an auto-enrolled account at [trumpaccounts.gov](https://trumpaccounts.gov) or through the official mobile app to manage investments, receive family contributions, and collect the $1,000 seed payment if your child is eligible. If you want your child to own equity today instead of waiting on future corporate deliveries, you can purchase shares in a custodial brokerage account opened by an adult. Read our guide on [how to buy SpaceX stock](/guides/how-to-buy-spacex-stock/) to review platform rules, private share access, and custody requirements.